"""cli/glosa -- glosa command-line interface (FOUNDATION_v0.3.md §9 "Callable layer" + S14 §9.1).

tier: finite_diagnostic (tests executed: `cli/glosa self-test`, `cli/glosa demo`, and
`cli/glosa check <path>` run against every file in `schema/examples/*.example.json` and
`schema/examples/fail/*.json` from the glosa repo root -- see cli/README.md for the exact
commands and their recorded output). Every dispatch/scaffolding decision this file makes beyond
what those runs actually exercised is Dr-tier, unreviewed, same as the rest of this repo --
readout-not-truth applies to this file's own header too.

stdlib argparse only. Imports kernel/glosa_kernel.py by RELATIVE PATH (this file's own directory's
sibling `kernel/`), never by package name, so the CLI works from any cwd once invoked as
`<repo>/cli/glosa` or `python3 <repo>/cli/glosa`. PyYAML is used OPTIONALLY for the human-facing
`.yaml` scaffold format; when it is not importable, every "new" command falls back to writing
`.json` instead and says so plainly in its own JSON result (never silently).

No network call anywhere in this file (same floor as the kernel, FOUNDATION §9). `cite check`
without `--offline` still performs only the offline schema+status check -- there is no live
Crossref/OpenAlex/PubMed/DataCite lookup implemented anywhere in this CLI; see `glosa cite check
--help` and cli/README.md's own "NOT IMPLEMENTED" note rather than trusting a command name alone.

Every command -- success, refusal, or error -- appends exactly one `{"kind": "tool_call", ...}`
line to `./logbook.jsonl` in the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY (not this file's directory), matching
`mcp/glosa_mcp_server.py`'s own logging contract (FOUNDATION §9: CLI and MCP are two callable
skins over the same kernel, and log the same way).
"""

